<title>SPAIN: Spain will meet three EMU criteria in 1997 - Barea.</title>
<headline>Spain will meet three EMU criteria in 1997 - Barea.</headline>
<dateline>PAMPLONA, Spain 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish Budget Secretary Jose Barea said on Thursday that Spain would fulfill single currency criteria on inflation, deficit and long-term rates in 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;We are in condition to reach the deficit objective in 1997. We will also fulfill the criteria on inflation and on rates,&quot; Barea told bankers at a seminar in this northern Spanish town.</p>
<p>As far as government debt to gross domestic product (GDP) goes, Barea said 1997 would be the first year that debt did not rise and instead, showed a tendency to decline.</p>
<p>Nonetheless, Barea added that debt, actually near 66 percent of GDP, would not be a determining criteria in the selection of single currency countries.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
